TEXT 0 -224 Left 2 ;Second-order band-pass (series RLC, output on R): H(s) = s ω0/Q / (s² + s ω0/Q + ω0²)\nω0 = 1/√(LC) = 31.6 krad/s (f0 ≈ 5.03 kHz) and Q = √(L/C) / R ≈ 2.1: two complex poles at −ω0/2Q ± jω0√(1 − 1/4Q²). A zero at s = 0.\nGain 1 (0 dB) at f0 and a bandwidth f0/Q ≈ 2.4 kHz between the −3 dB points; ±20 dB/decade far from f0 and a phase from +90° to −90°.\nStep: a damped oscillation that starts and ends at 0.
